- **ALURELAB NextAuth CSRF Fix**: Node.js 20.x encodes `|` to `%7C` in Set-Cookie headers, breaking NextAuth v5 beta.32 CSRF token verification (`token|hash` format). Two server-side patches in `@auth/core` (persisted via `postinstall`): (1) `csrf-token.js`: decode `%7C` before splitting cookie value; (2) `index.js`: parse `ReadableStream` body for App Router compatibility. Also removed `auth()` middleware wrapper from `middleware.ts` to prevent double CSRF token generation. Credentials login flow uses `/api/auth/callback/credentials` (not `/signin/credentials`). Backup: `/home/alurelab/app.alurelab.com.bak_20260916_middleware/`.
